Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:41:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] zink: destroy the resource object's copy lock

resource_object_create initialises obj->copy_lock with u_rwlock_init,
and nothing destroyed it. With glibc that costs nothing, the lock living
in the object. On the PS4 an initialised pthread rwlock holds 64 bytes
of libkernel's pthread pool until it is destroyed, and that pool is
fixed: the orbis-ports mesa-ps4 port counted 146 rwlocks created a frame
and none destroyed, all from here, until the title died with
"[ScePthread/System] Internal Memory is running out".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bb93U7uY5qVNuEcHDggEfE
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
index c37fa55..65b8b58 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -223,6 +223,7 @@ zink_destroy_resource_object(struct zink_screen *screen, struct zink_resource_ob
    if (!obj->dt)
       zink_destroy_resource_surface_cache(screen, &obj->surface_cache, obj->is_buffer);
    simple_mtx_destroy(&obj->surface_mtx);
+   u_rwlock_destroy(&obj->copy_lock);
    if (!obj->dt && zink_debug & ZINK_DEBUG_MEM)
       zink_debug_mem_del(screen, obj->bo);
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(obj->copies); i++)
